**Communication → Notice Board** is where the school posts notices that stay visible, as opposed to
[Send Messages](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-send-messages), which sends a one-off SMS. A notice can reach
staff, parents (who are also notified on their phones the first time it is published) or the
parents and teachers of selected classes.

## Reading notices

Everyone on the staff side can read the board (the *View the notice board* permission). The **Board**
tab lists the notices that apply to you, newest first, with pinned notices at the top.
*No notices right now.* means there are none.

## Posting notices

Posting is a separate permission (*Create, publish, pin & archive notices*) that the defaults leave
with the administrator, because it puts text in front of the whole school. If you have it, the page
also has a **Manage** tab with every notice and a **New notice** button.

1. Select **New notice**.
2. Enter a **Title** and a **Message**. Both are required (*Give the notice a title.*, *Write the
   message.*), and each has a length limit.
3. Choose the **Audience**: everyone, teachers, parents, or **classes**. For classes, pick which ones.
   Parents of children in those classes, and the teachers who teach them, will see the notice. A user
   with no assigned class has no class to post to.
4. Set **Publish** to a date and time. A future time schedules the notice.
5. Optionally set **Expires**. The expiry must be after the publication date.
6. Optionally attach a PDF or an image (up to 20 MB each). Attachments can be added from the web app
   only.
7. Choose **Save draft**, or **Publish**. Editing an existing notice offers **Save** and **Save &
   publish**.

You will see *Notice saved*.

## Managing notices

The **Manage** tab lists **Title**, **Audience**, **Status**, **Dates** and **Files**, and can be
filtered by status: **Drafts**, **Published** or **Archived**. On each row you can:

- **Edit** the notice.
- **Publish** a draft. A dialog confirms the audience first; parents are notified if the notice
  hasn't been sent before.
- **Pin to the top** or **Unpin**.
- **Archive** it.

Status chips tell you where a notice is: **Draft**, **Scheduled** (publication date in the future),
**Live**, **Expired** or **Archived**.

